<description>
Render the lower grey slot array by replacing each colored control pixel with the matching legend template.

Input structure
A background grid has a top legend: each colored marker sits one row above and one column left of a
2x2 template drawn in a shared template ink color.  Below it is a rectangular array of 2x2 grey slots,
where a slot may contain one colored control pixel in place of grey.

Rule
Read the legend as color -> 2x2 template mask.  Convert the lower slot array into a compact array with
the same row/column layout and one background separator row/column between neighboring tiles.  Empty
grey slots become blank tiles; a colored slot becomes that color's legend mask recolored with the
control color.

Key insight
The colored pixel in a grey slot names which top legend template to stamp; its position inside the slot
is irrelevant.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "colored control pixels inside lower 2x2 grey slots s",
  "dst": "top legend 2x2 template masks d",
  "match_cond": "s.color == d.marker_color",
  "transform": "replace each lower slot with d.mask recolored to s.color in the compact output lattice; slots without a control pixel become background",
  "grid_shape": "lower R x C slot array -> (2R+R-1) x (2C+C-1) output with one background separator row/column",
  "symbol_instructions": "top legend maps each colored marker to the adjacent 2x2 template mask"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  background: 0
  slot_color: 5 (grey)
  template_ink: 1
  legend:
    position: top of grid, markers on one row, templates in 2 rows below
    num_entries: 3-4 distinct marker colors
    marker: single pixel at (r, c); template at (r+1:r+3, c+1:c+3)
    template_mask: 2x2 binary, 3 or 4 cells filled; exactly 1 full (4/4), rest L-shaped (3/4)
    all masks distinct within an example
    horizontal_spacing: 4-5 cols between consecutive markers (uniform within example)
  slot_array:
    dimensions: 3-4 rows x 4-5 cols of 2x2 blocks
    block_spacing: 3 (2 cell block + 1 bg separator) in both axes
    gap_above: 2-4 blank rows between legend bottom and first slot row
    control_pixel: always at local position (1,1) within 2x2 slot
    fill_ratio: 58-67% of slots have a control pixel; rest are solid grey
    every marker color used in slots appears in legend; not all legend colors need appear in slots [observed]
  grid: 17-20 rows x 18-20 cols
  output:
    size: (2R + R-1) x (2C + C-1) where RxC is slot array dimensions
    each slot becomes 2x2 tile; bg separator between tiles
    filled slot -> template mask recolored with control color; empty slot -> all bg

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick slot array dims R=3-4, C=4-5 and N=3-4 legend entries
    2. Choose N distinct marker colors and assign each a distinct 2x2 mask (exactly one 4/4, rest 3/4 L-shaped)
    3. Build the output grid (2R+R-1) x (2C+C-1); for each slot position randomly assign a marker color or leave empty (targeting ~60% fill)
    4. Stamp template masks recolored with control color into output tiles
    5. Derive the input: place legend at top (marker + ink templates), leave gap rows, then lay out RxC slot array with 2x2 grey blocks; inject control pixel at (1,1) of each filled slot, pad grid with bg
```
