  "summary": "Complete the dominant-color mask by adding its horizontal mirror image.",
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "mask of the uniquely most frequent color",
  "dst": "mirror cells across the grid's vertical centerline",
  "transform": "paint each mirrored cell with the source color; preserve all existing pixels elsewhere"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed]
  colors: exactly 4 distinct colors; one is the dominant (most frequent) foreground color
  dominant_color:
    count_in_input: 30-34, strictly most frequent (gap to 2nd >= 3)
    mask: LR-symmetric in output; NOT LR-symmetric in input
    shape: connected blob spanning 6-8 rows, centered at vertical midline (col 4.5)
    row_widths: even integers 2-10, not necessarily monotonic; may have internal gaps
    blob_output_size: 36-48 cells
  noise:
    description: in input, some right-half cells of the symmetric blob are replaced by non-dominant colors
    location: exclusively in right half (cols 5-9); left half is intact
    count: 6-14 cells (15-58% of right-half blob area)
    values: drawn from the 3 non-dominant colors (random mix)
  background:
    region: all cells outside the symmetric blob outline
    content: random mix of the 3 non-dominant colors; dominant color never appears here
    preserved: identical between input and output
  transform: mirror left-half dominant mask to right half, painting over noise cells

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 4 distinct colors; designate one as dominant (D).
    2. On a 10x10 grid, design an LR-symmetric connected blob of D (36-48 cells, spanning 6-8 rows). For each active row, pick an even width (2-10) centered at col 4.5; optionally add symmetric internal gaps. Ensure the blob is connected.
    3. Fill all non-blob cells with a random mix of the 3 non-dominant colors. This is the output grid.
    4. To make the input, select 6-14 right-half blob cells and replace them with random non-dominant colors. Ensure the dominant color remains strictly most frequent (gap >= 3) and the left half is unchanged.
    5. Verify dominant color is not LR-symmetric in the input (it should not be, since right-half cells were removed).
```
